<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Federated Shan States</h1><p class="st-meta">1922 CE – 1948 CE · capital Taunggyi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British union of more than thirty Shan and other hereditary states of eastern Burma, created in 1922 and governed from Taunggyi.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1922 the British combined the protected Shan states and the Wa states under a federal council, separating them from ministerial <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/myanmar">Burma</a> when the Dyarchy reforms gave the province partial self-government. The commissioner was based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taunggyi">Taunggyi</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The saophas kept their hereditary positions and authority over local affairs, while a British commissioner controlled policing, finances and public works through a Federal Council of Chiefs. A common budget funded roads and schools. The federation remained separate from the parliamentary system set up in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/myanmar">Burma</a> in 1937. Japanese and Thai forces occupied the area in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panglong-conference">Panglong Conference</a> of 1947 Shan leaders agreed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san">Aung San</a> to join an independent <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/myanmar">Burma</a>, and the Federated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shan-state">Shan States</a> became Shan State of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> in 1948.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/federated-shan-states.jpg" alt="Federated Shan States" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: derivative work from Flag of Myanmar.svg · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Shan_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1922 CE – 1948 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Taunggyi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Shan, Burmese, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Myanmar</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Shan States</dd></dl></aside></div>
